    "description": "I worked for FarmWorks Software on a desktop and mobile GIS application written in C++ adding new features, changing databases, and designing UI.  I worked on porting the software from our older Borland compiler to Microsoft Visual C++.\n\nIn July 2009, the company was acquired by Trimble, and we began working on an online website written in C#, using Silverlight, and RIA Services for database access.\n\nI also assisted in transition the website to a DurandalJS single page application rewrite, with a C# REST API backend using entity framework.  After Trimble acquired another company which had their own website, I helped architect and implement the core login and UI infrastructure to help merge the two websites.",
